A||||3||Dough19||FWD 3.4 oil pan||||1||
Z||000000||Dough19||12-22-2001||03:52 PM||||I'm in the process of doing a FWD 3.4 swap out of a 99 Olds Alero on my 88GT. I want to use the aluminum pan, but I'm not sure which front timing chain cover will seal to it. For anyone who has done this, which one did you use, and were there any other mods that you had to do to get it to work? Thanks <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/yellow101/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/yellow101/fiero.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe Torma||12-22-2001||04:05 PM||||Another 3400 swap!<P>I made my own mount that bolts under the pan(stock location).  It uses the original plate and extends over the cradle, where the new mount is. this is so I could use the 3400 front cover.  Others have used the stock Fiero stuff.  The advantages to the 3400 cover...lest see...20 minute waterpump change, 30 second belt change and a cleaner look<P>The engine already has 9.5:1 compression...have you checked valve/piston clearances?  gotta be close.  Are you using the Fiero intake or the 3400 intake?<P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dough19||12-22-2001||04:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>Another 3400 swap!<P>I made my own mount that bolts under the pan(stock location).  It uses the original plate and extends over the cradle, where the new mount is. this is so I could use the 3400 front cover.  Others have used the stock Fiero stuff.  The advantages to the 3400 cover...lest see...20 minute waterpump change, 30 second belt change and a cleaner look<P>The engine already has 9.5:1 compression...have you checked valve/piston clearances?  gotta be close.  Are you using the Fiero intake or the 3400 intake?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I guess I should have clearified my question a little more. I am using the fiero intake, heads, etc.  So I need to know what Fiero front timing cover I need.  Sorry about that.<BR>I really didn't want to do the wiring mods to use the complete motor.  And even if I did I probably would have just went ahead and got a 3.8.  So I sold the intake and heads on ebay -sure makes the block cost a lot less  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Neal||12-22-2001||08:34 PM||||Im 99% sure that you use the stock 87-88 timing chain cover.<P>Just dry fit it and youll know for sure right away||||reg||1
